Task 1: Understanding DevSecOps Maturity Model Framework
Subtask 1.1: Introduction to DevSecOps Maturity Model
The DevSecOps Maturity Model provides a structured approach to assess and improve security integration within DevOps practices. It defines four maturity levels:

Level 1 - Basic: Initial security awareness with manual processes Level 2 - Managed: Defined security processes with some automation Level 3 - Defined: Standardized security practices across teams Level 4 - Optimized: Continuous improvement with advanced automation

